1
00:00:00,234 --> 00:00:01,602
I can't let you do this.

2
00:00:01,602 --> 00:00:03,404
I love him, Dad.

3
00:00:03,404 --> 00:00:04,501
Because of Liam.

4
00:00:04,501 --> 00:00:08,142
I hold on to my life
because of what he made me feel.

5
00:00:08,142 --> 00:00:10,211
Bad day? It feels good to breathe!

6
00:00:10,211 --> 00:00:14,515
- It feels good to breathe!
- More!

7
00:00:14,515 --> 00:00:17,018
- That's it!
- Hi, Maxine.

8
00:00:17,018 --> 00:00:18,553
You look good.

9
00:00:18,553 --> 00:00:19,887
Well, congrats.

10
00:00:19,887 --> 00:00:23,830
I heard they're considering you
to star in the new prime time show.

11
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:25,460
This will be your big break.

12
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:27,362
Yes, Sir Pao.

13
00:00:27,362 --> 00:00:30,131
You know how showbiz is.
Everyone has his own time.

14
00:00:30,131 --> 00:00:33,167
Where's Sir Liam? So you can go home.

15
00:00:33,167 --> 00:00:36,237
Miss Joyce, I was with Sir Liam
outside earlier

16
00:00:36,237 --> 00:00:38,039
while waiting for the props.

17
00:00:38,039 --> 00:00:40,708
But when I returned to greet the suppliers,

18
00:00:40,708 --> 00:00:42,410
Sir Liam wasn't there anymore.

19
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:43,678
Lift him up.

20
00:00:43,678 --> 00:00:45,446
Call the medic!

21
00:00:45,446 --> 00:00:46,660
Medic!

22
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:48,349
- Via!
- Spoiled brat!

23
00:00:48,349 --> 00:00:50,251
Dad, please. Don't, no, please.

24
00:00:50,251 --> 00:00:52,041
I love him!

25
00:00:52,041 --> 00:00:53,054
From now on,

26
00:00:53,054 --> 00:00:56,724
you are no longer connected
in any of my businesses.

27
00:00:56,724 --> 00:00:59,227
I was kicked out from
the Herrera Group of Companies.

28
00:00:59,227 --> 00:01:00,628
I'm no longer part of Blacksmith.

29
00:01:00,628 --> 00:01:02,797
I can't go back to Casa Fuerte either.

30
00:01:02,797 --> 00:01:04,599
What about our film?

31
00:01:04,599 --> 00:01:07,468
I have no choice but to start over again.

32
00:01:07,468 --> 00:01:10,204
Why don't we make our own film?

33
00:01:10,204 --> 00:01:15,009
On one condition.
Part of what we'll make from the movie

34
00:01:15,009 --> 00:01:16,894
will go to this orphanage.

35
00:01:16,894 --> 00:01:18,246
I won't say no to that.

36
00:01:18,246 --> 00:01:20,541
- Deal?
- Deal.

37
00:01:36,498 --> 00:01:38,833
What's the occasion?

38
00:01:39,634 --> 00:01:42,970
Someone special is coming over.

39
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:45,339
Too bad Borj isn't here.

40
00:01:45,339 --> 00:01:47,542
I cooked a lot.

41
00:01:47,542 --> 00:01:50,478
Special? It looks special, son.

42
00:01:50,478 --> 00:01:53,415
It has lots of onions.

43
00:01:53,415 --> 00:01:55,316
Onions are expensive nowadays.

44
00:01:55,316 --> 00:01:59,419
So, special, huh? Who is it?

45
00:02:01,122 --> 00:02:03,825
Nothing. Just a guest, Mom.

46
00:02:03,825 --> 00:02:05,059
Just a guest.

47
00:02:05,059 --> 00:02:06,494
It's just a colleague.

48
00:02:06,494 --> 00:02:07,728
My colleague.

49
00:02:07,728 --> 00:02:09,397
- Colleague?
- Yes.

50
00:02:10,498 --> 00:02:11,833
Colleague?

51
00:02:11,833 --> 00:02:13,701
Smells like you showered in perfume.

52
00:02:13,701 --> 00:02:16,136
Is it really just a colleague?

53
00:02:17,004 --> 00:02:18,473
Hello!

54
00:02:18,473 --> 00:02:22,136
- Oh, hello!
- Wow, lots of food...

55
00:02:22,136 --> 00:02:23,878
Yes.

56
00:02:23,878 --> 00:02:25,646
How are you?

57
00:02:25,646 --> 00:02:26,714
- This is Queenie, Auntie.
- Yes.

58
00:02:26,714 --> 00:02:28,916
- Hello, Queenie.
- Hello, Ma'am Tess.

59
00:02:28,916 --> 00:02:30,384
- Right...
- What's the occasion?

60
00:02:30,384 --> 00:02:34,355
So that's why my son showered in perfume.

61
00:02:34,355 --> 00:02:36,357
It's because you're coming.

62
00:02:36,357 --> 00:02:38,059
He even cooked for you.

63
00:02:38,059 --> 00:02:40,161
Look at that.

64
00:02:40,161 --> 00:02:44,965
I remember the young love, sweet love.

65
00:02:45,833 --> 00:02:47,673
What's the occasion?

66
00:02:48,536 --> 00:02:51,439
Wait, don't you know about this, Via?

67
00:02:51,439 --> 00:02:54,442
No. Is this a surprise?

68
00:02:54,442 --> 00:02:57,477
Who's the special guest?

69
00:02:58,579 --> 00:03:00,547
Special?

70
00:03:04,285 --> 00:03:06,353
Anybody home?

71
00:03:11,759 --> 00:03:18,099
Sorry, we let ourselves in
because your door is open.

72
00:03:18,099 --> 00:03:19,901
- Sorry, Auntie.
- Joyce.

73
00:03:19,901 --> 00:03:22,035
Hi, Aunt Tess.

74
00:03:23,137 --> 00:03:24,272
It's okay.

75
00:03:24,272 --> 00:03:25,940
Via.

76
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:27,541
Come on in. Come in.

77
00:03:27,541 --> 00:03:29,620
We welcome ourselves.

78
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:31,546
Oh, I have a gift for you.

79
00:03:31,546 --> 00:03:34,026
- For me?
- Yes. Here.

80
00:03:34,026 --> 00:03:36,550
This is for good luck,
good life, and long life.

81
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:38,152
Oh?

82
00:03:38,152 --> 00:03:40,588
- Wow!
- What's your year?

83
00:03:40,588 --> 00:03:43,112
- Horse.
- Oh, horse.

84
00:03:46,627 --> 00:03:48,663
- Wow.
- Hold on.

85
00:03:48,663 --> 00:03:52,233
Ma'am Tess, be careful with...

86
00:03:52,233 --> 00:03:53,401
Horses!

87
00:03:53,401 --> 00:03:55,603
- Really?
- Yes, with horses...

88
00:03:55,603 --> 00:03:58,105
- Horses?
- I mean with an ironing board.

89
00:03:58,105 --> 00:04:00,474
Let's save the jokes for later, Odet.

90
00:04:00,474 --> 00:04:03,894
We should eat first.

91
00:04:04,979 --> 00:04:07,682
So, you're the special guest.

92
00:04:07,682 --> 00:04:10,818
That's why Liam was so busy.

93
00:04:10,818 --> 00:04:13,854
He couldn't even answer my call.

94
00:04:13,854 --> 00:04:15,022
You're lucky.

95
00:04:15,022 --> 00:04:17,237
Auntie Tess is the one who usually cooks.

96
00:04:17,237 --> 00:04:18,693
Right, Auntie?

97
00:04:18,693 --> 00:04:23,998
It's his first time cooking.
My boyfriend has never cooked for me.

98
00:04:23,998 --> 00:04:26,801
I hope you don't get a stomach ache.

99
00:04:28,336 --> 00:04:30,371
I don't think so.

100
00:04:30,371 --> 00:04:32,919
Did you cook a lot, Liam?

101
00:04:34,175 --> 00:04:37,044
Why? Are there other people coming?

102
00:04:37,044 --> 00:04:39,846
Is Hans with you?

103
00:04:43,351 --> 00:04:44,485
Hi!

104
00:04:44,485 --> 00:04:46,053
Hello.

105
00:04:46,053 --> 00:04:48,055
What are you guys doing here?

106
00:04:48,055 --> 00:04:49,624
Liam...

107
00:04:49,624 --> 00:04:51,525
Like me...

108
00:04:51,525 --> 00:04:54,261
They also can't leave you.

109
00:05:21,689 --> 00:05:24,692
Let's continue our project.

110
00:05:24,692 --> 00:05:30,026
We're all here because we all agreed.

111
00:05:30,898 --> 00:05:32,733
We were off to a good start.

112
00:05:32,733 --> 00:05:34,835
Right, guys?

113
00:05:34,835 --> 00:05:38,506
But VLH called it trash.

114
00:05:38,506 --> 00:05:39,907
He wanted to brings things back
to the old formula...

115
00:05:39,907 --> 00:05:42,909
Blacksmith producing action films.

116
00:05:43,744 --> 00:05:45,446
What will happen
to the sequences already shot?

117
00:05:45,446 --> 00:05:49,128
Miss Joyce paid for all of it.

118
00:05:51,003 --> 00:05:52,586
Let's not talk about money.

119
00:05:52,586 --> 00:05:55,256
Let's just charge it to experience.

120
00:05:55,256 --> 00:05:57,980
That experience is so expensive.

121
00:06:00,961 --> 00:06:03,163
So, Liam...

122
00:06:04,401 --> 00:06:06,368
Are you game?

123
00:06:07,802 --> 00:06:11,772
As long as it's not for propaganda.

124
00:06:11,772 --> 00:06:13,874
I mean...

125
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:16,577
I know you're concerned
about the elections, Josh, but...

126
00:06:16,577 --> 00:06:18,212
I know you're going to say that.

127
00:06:18,212 --> 00:06:21,549
So I already prepared an answer.

128
00:06:21,549 --> 00:06:23,284
This time...

129
00:06:23,284 --> 00:06:28,352
we don't have to rush or finish
before the elections.

130
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:32,692
We can release it after the elections, right?

131
00:06:35,563 --> 00:06:37,131
Sir Liam,

132
00:06:37,131 --> 00:06:42,602
maybe this can help us not become unemployed.

133
00:06:44,805 --> 00:06:49,343
If everything is all good...

134
00:06:49,343 --> 00:06:51,612
Then, game!

135
00:06:51,612 --> 00:06:53,767
- Right?
- That's what we want to hear.

136
00:06:57,118 --> 00:06:58,652
What else is missing?

137
00:06:58,652 --> 00:07:00,389
Your work.

138
00:07:01,255 --> 00:07:04,492
New story, Liam.

139
00:07:04,492 --> 00:07:06,660
Do you already have an idea?

140
00:07:13,033 --> 00:07:15,136
Love story.

141
00:07:15,136 --> 00:07:17,223
Love story.

142
00:07:30,218 --> 00:07:31,723
Cake?

143
00:07:40,127 --> 00:07:42,262
Yes, please.

144
00:07:44,064 --> 00:07:46,167
Do you want some, too?

145
00:07:46,167 --> 00:07:47,368
- Yes?
- Sure.

146
00:07:47,368 --> 00:07:50,371
Try it. Come on. Try it first.

147
00:07:50,371 --> 00:07:53,006
- I got it. Let me.
- Come on.

148
00:07:57,845 --> 00:08:00,941
Oops, I'm sorry.

149
00:08:04,585 --> 00:08:07,822
Well, actually, this concept isn't new.

150
00:08:07,822 --> 00:08:14,628
I mean, most of us want a love story.

151
00:08:15,729 --> 00:08:17,832
A story that has...

152
00:08:17,832 --> 00:08:20,534
What else could it be?

153
00:08:20,534 --> 00:08:26,139
A happy... ending.

154
00:08:28,342 --> 00:08:30,039
But...

155
00:08:31,345 --> 00:08:33,914
does the story really end here?

156
00:08:33,914 --> 00:08:36,750
I mean, for example...

157
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:40,955
When both sides of the family

158
00:08:40,955 --> 00:08:44,925
already agree to the forbidden love
of our heroes...

159
00:08:44,925 --> 00:08:51,265
Or, if the leading man catches up
with the woman at the airport

160
00:08:51,265 --> 00:08:53,534
right before she leaves...

161
00:08:53,534 --> 00:08:59,607
Or when they already said their vows
at the altar...

162
00:08:59,607 --> 00:09:03,410
What's next to their love story?

163
00:09:03,410 --> 00:09:10,450
What really happens after happily ever after?

164
00:09:11,485 --> 00:09:14,088
That won't be easy, Sir.

165
00:09:14,088 --> 00:09:16,323
You know why?

166
00:09:16,323 --> 00:09:24,298
I will show you what will happen
after the happily ever after.

167
00:09:24,298 --> 00:09:26,934
Let's go, Megan. Come with me.

168
00:09:26,934 --> 00:09:27,968
Just come with me.

169
00:09:27,968 --> 00:09:29,470
Me?

170
00:09:29,470 --> 00:09:30,804
Okay, let's see.

171
00:09:30,804 --> 00:09:32,605
Stay here.

172
00:09:34,608 --> 00:09:37,310
Watch this.

173
00:09:39,013 --> 00:09:43,390
Babe, come on. Just once.

174
00:09:43,390 --> 00:09:44,952
Stop messing with me.

175
00:09:44,952 --> 00:09:47,154
Come on, Babe.

176
00:09:47,154 --> 00:09:49,336
Let's make love.

177
00:09:49,336 --> 00:09:52,760
Let's give our son a sibling. Come on.

178
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:55,362
Let's go, Babe.

179
00:09:55,362 --> 00:09:56,997
Hey, Leopoldo.

180
00:09:56,997 --> 00:09:58,699
How dare you.

181
00:09:58,699 --> 00:10:02,536
You don't give enough money
for diapers and milk.

182
00:10:02,536 --> 00:10:05,422
And now, you want another child?

183
00:10:08,008 --> 00:10:09,310
End scene.

184
00:10:09,310 --> 00:10:10,611
See?

185
00:10:10,611 --> 00:10:12,212
The story arc is so drastic.

186
00:10:12,212 --> 00:10:15,516
Before, they would kiss each other
the moment they touched.

187
00:10:15,516 --> 00:10:18,018
But now, look at what happened.

188
00:10:18,018 --> 00:10:20,354
Or it can also be like this.

189
00:10:20,354 --> 00:10:25,025
In the first act, their hearts beat faster...

190
00:10:25,025 --> 00:10:26,727
from fear.

191
00:10:26,727 --> 00:10:29,475
Hurry up! The zombies are coming!

192
00:10:32,633 --> 00:10:33,968
Love...

193
00:10:33,968 --> 00:10:35,803
Go on and run.

194
00:10:35,803 --> 00:10:36,837
Leave me here.

195
00:10:36,837 --> 00:10:37,870
- No.
- Go.

196
00:10:37,870 --> 00:10:41,207
- Hurry, go!
- I won't leave you. I love you so much.

197
00:10:43,649 --> 00:10:45,645
Did you get bitten?

198
00:10:48,048 --> 00:10:49,883
He got bitten.

199
00:10:56,890 --> 00:10:58,659
Me, too! I want to get bitten!

200
00:10:58,659 --> 00:11:01,027
I want to get bitten.

201
00:11:04,865 --> 00:11:06,734
That's enough.

202
00:11:06,734 --> 00:11:09,002
Stop. Cut! Cut!

203
00:11:09,870 --> 00:11:11,338
- End scene.
- I love it!

204
00:11:11,338 --> 00:11:12,740
I got carried away.

205
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:13,941
- It's good.
- That's it.

206
00:11:13,941 --> 00:11:17,444
Nice. We can do that.

207
00:11:17,444 --> 00:11:19,513
- Nice!
- That's good. That's okay.

208
00:11:19,513 --> 00:11:20,514
I love it.

209
00:11:20,514 --> 00:11:24,852
Sir Liam, I'm sure Joyce has ideas too.

210
00:11:24,852 --> 00:11:26,253
Go on, Sis. Come on. Pitch your ideas.

211
00:11:26,253 --> 00:11:27,554
- We're just the only ones here.
- No.

212
00:11:27,554 --> 00:11:28,956
- Go on.
- Why me?

213
00:11:28,956 --> 00:11:31,592
Go, sis. Show them your acting prowess.

214
00:11:31,592 --> 00:11:32,793
Go, Joyce.

215
00:11:32,793 --> 00:11:34,361
Go, Joyce.

216
00:11:36,430 --> 00:11:38,794
- Go, Joyce.
- Go, Joyce.

217
00:11:49,143 --> 00:11:51,110
They say...

218
00:11:53,273 --> 00:11:55,274
They say, if...

219
00:11:56,761 --> 00:12:00,330
if two people can't grow together, they...

220
00:12:01,088 --> 00:12:03,424
they grow apart.

221
00:12:03,424 --> 00:12:06,459
I thought it wouldn't happen to us.

222
00:12:08,396 --> 00:12:13,233
I won't regret that
we did not give up until the end.

223
00:12:17,638 --> 00:12:19,973
Even in the next life...

224
00:12:21,642 --> 00:12:24,377
or in the life after that...

225
00:12:26,647 --> 00:12:29,616
I will still love you.

226
00:12:32,803 --> 00:12:35,355
I still love you so much.

227
00:13:06,587 --> 00:13:09,523
Even though in the end...

228
00:13:22,428 --> 00:13:25,339
That's all.

229
00:13:25,339 --> 00:13:27,742
Beautiful.

230
00:13:30,813 --> 00:13:32,267
You really are something, Sis.

231
00:13:33,347 --> 00:13:34,792
You have my vote, sis.

232
00:13:34,792 --> 00:13:38,286
But if happily ever after doesn't exist...

233
00:13:38,286 --> 00:13:41,222
He can still find new love.

234
00:13:41,222 --> 00:13:43,057
Right, Love?

235
00:13:56,371 --> 00:13:59,874
But if happily ever after doesn't exist...

236
00:13:59,874 --> 00:14:02,811
He can still find new love.

237
00:14:02,811 --> 00:14:04,645
Right, Love?

238
00:14:11,886 --> 00:14:15,614
For me, love is a choice.

239
00:14:16,825 --> 00:14:19,559
If it doesn't work out with someone,

240
00:14:19,559 --> 00:14:23,562
you can always choose
to be happy with someone else.

241
00:14:26,266 --> 00:14:28,401
I agree.

242
00:14:28,401 --> 00:14:32,104
As long as you are breathing, there's hope.

243
00:14:35,775 --> 00:14:37,911
So...

244
00:14:37,911 --> 00:14:40,546
Love triangle?

245
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:42,347
Why not?

246
00:14:43,950 --> 00:14:49,389
But he should... stand by his new love.

247
00:14:49,389 --> 00:14:51,557
It's toxic.

248
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:57,262
They keep trying even if they get hurt
over and over again.

249
00:14:59,265 --> 00:15:05,137
So the hero will end up with his new love?

250
00:15:08,308 --> 00:15:09,609
Sorry, I just got carried away.

251
00:15:09,609 --> 00:15:11,244
That's nice.

252
00:15:11,244 --> 00:15:14,813
- That's good.
- Woman empowerment, right?

253
00:15:16,115 --> 00:15:18,650
If it's a story about women,

254
00:15:19,252 --> 00:15:23,455
the woman will be happy even if she's alone.

255
00:15:24,991 --> 00:15:26,792
She's free.

256
00:15:28,167 --> 00:15:32,037
She will let the two be happy.

257
00:15:34,367 --> 00:15:36,426
I love it.

258
00:15:39,138 --> 00:15:41,140
I love it too.

259
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:44,277
We'll teach about self-love.

260
00:15:44,277 --> 00:15:48,680
But at the same time,
the value of commitment.

261
00:15:50,705 --> 00:15:53,007
What do you think, Sir Liam?

262
00:16:01,461 --> 00:16:04,630
All your ideas are valid.

263
00:16:05,565 --> 00:16:12,504
But I guess...
the central theme of our story...

264
00:16:14,007 --> 00:16:17,009
will be about second chances.

265
00:16:18,411 --> 00:16:21,547
I mean, when it comes to relationships,

266
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:28,053
there will be problems.

267
00:16:29,022 --> 00:16:30,956
Challenges...

268
00:16:33,359 --> 00:16:39,031
But we will show how they will face it...

269
00:16:40,233 --> 00:16:42,070
together.

270
00:16:57,552 --> 00:16:59,520
Dance your heart out?

271
00:17:00,853 --> 00:17:03,088
This is all I could give, Joyce.

272
00:17:07,666 --> 00:17:09,119
You can do it.

273
00:17:10,396 --> 00:17:12,031
Miss Lemon...

274
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:16,702
Miss Lemon, thank you so much
for letting us pitch our concept

275
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:19,405
to you and to Miss Charry for DigiTV.

276
00:17:19,405 --> 00:17:22,608
Oh, come on. I love your story, Joyce.

277
00:17:22,608 --> 00:17:25,044
And I love your script, Liam.

278
00:17:25,044 --> 00:17:27,947
Gosh! Love it, love it, love it!

279
00:17:27,947 --> 00:17:30,783
Because I lived it!

280
00:17:30,783 --> 00:17:32,885
It's so painful.

281
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:39,459
You know, it's painful but heartwarming, too.

282
00:17:39,459 --> 00:17:41,461
Miss Charry's just in Singapore right now.

283
00:17:41,461 --> 00:17:45,965
But she wanted you to know that
she could relate to your story.

284
00:17:45,965 --> 00:17:47,633
Thank you.

285
00:17:47,633 --> 00:17:51,938
You know, guys, we at DigiTV are down
for great Filipino love stories.

286
00:17:51,938 --> 00:17:55,007
Especially "What Happens
After Happily Ever After"?

287
00:17:55,007 --> 00:17:58,811
Millennials and Gen Z
will definitely watch it.

288
00:17:58,811 --> 00:18:04,283
And that's what the young viewers like.

289
00:18:04,283 --> 00:18:07,320
But... just an idea.

290
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:11,491
Why don't we put
an out-of-the-country element?

291
00:18:11,491 --> 00:18:16,295
Let's go out of the Philippines,
so we can reach the Filipinos abroad.

292
00:18:17,196 --> 00:18:19,599
Why? Budget concerns?

293
00:18:19,599 --> 00:18:21,167
Don't worry.

294
00:18:21,167 --> 00:18:24,549
We'll talk to the embassy
of whatever country you'll choose

295
00:18:24,549 --> 00:18:27,606
so we can save some money, right?

296
00:18:29,342 --> 00:18:33,334
Miss Lemon, thank you so much.
You are heaven-sent to us.

297
00:18:33,334 --> 00:18:38,351
Actually, Miss Lemon,
our concept is flexible.

298
00:18:38,351 --> 00:18:43,890
It will still work even if we transpose it
to another place.

299
00:18:43,890 --> 00:18:45,625
Don't worry.

300
00:18:45,625 --> 00:18:52,153
We'll adjust the script
and we'll get back to you.

301
00:18:54,001 --> 00:18:55,461
Now you're talking.

302
00:18:55,461 --> 00:18:59,472
Miss Lemon... thank you so much.

303
00:18:59,472 --> 00:19:05,278
It's been my dream to make a film on DigiTV.

304
00:19:05,278 --> 00:19:08,014
Come on. It's my pleasure.

305
00:19:08,014 --> 00:19:11,184
But I only have one request.

306
00:19:11,184 --> 00:19:14,287
- What is it?
- What is it?

307
00:19:14,287 --> 00:19:19,292
Can you make one of my artists
part of your film?

308
00:19:19,292 --> 00:19:20,693
Who is it, Miss Lemon?

309
00:19:20,693 --> 00:19:22,695
Oh, you know her very well.

310
00:19:22,695 --> 00:19:24,784
It's Maxine.

311
00:19:25,999 --> 00:19:27,634
Sorry.

312
00:19:27,634 --> 00:19:30,202
Do you have an issue?

313
00:19:32,203 --> 00:19:34,730
Not at all, Miss Lemon.

314
00:19:34,730 --> 00:19:36,865
We don't have any issues.

315
00:19:41,615 --> 00:19:43,717
Actually, it's perfect, Miss Lemon.

316
00:19:43,717 --> 00:19:49,122
We're looking for another female lead
because it's a love triangle...

317
00:19:49,122 --> 00:19:51,057
Then that's it!

318
00:19:51,057 --> 00:19:52,225
That's great.

319
00:19:52,225 --> 00:19:53,793
Stay there.

320
00:19:53,793 --> 00:19:54,961
This is just a warm-up.

321
00:19:54,961 --> 00:19:56,796
Come on. Join us.

322
00:19:56,796 --> 00:19:58,031
- Game.
- This is just a warm-up?

323
00:19:58,031 --> 00:19:59,166
Yes.

324
00:19:59,166 --> 00:20:01,535
There. There.

325
00:20:01,535 --> 00:20:03,970
So this is just a warm-up, Joyce.

326
00:20:03,970 --> 00:20:06,973
Turn, turn, turn.

327
00:20:06,973 --> 00:20:08,308
I'm sweating profusely, Joyce.

328
00:20:08,308 --> 00:20:11,044
Just do it.
We don't want to lose our project.

329
00:20:11,044 --> 00:20:12,487
- Lower.
- Lower?

330
00:20:12,487 --> 00:20:14,080
So we're going down.

331
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,215
There, lower.

332
00:20:15,215 --> 00:20:17,317
- Lower? Lower?
- Yes, yes.

333
00:20:17,317 --> 00:20:20,820
- It hurts my knees.
- Good job!

334
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:22,155
Sway. Shake your hips.

335
00:20:22,155 --> 00:20:23,757
Sway?

336
00:20:23,757 --> 00:20:26,260
- A lot is happening.
- One, two, three, four.

337
00:20:26,260 --> 00:20:28,596
One, two, three, four.

338
00:20:28,596 --> 00:20:29,930
There you go.

339
00:20:33,934 --> 00:20:35,835
Have you been waiting long?

340
00:20:38,172 --> 00:20:40,340
You're quiet.

341
00:20:41,208 --> 00:20:44,077
Where is the man we're going to meet?

342
00:20:47,381 --> 00:20:48,716
Why are you here?

343
00:20:48,716 --> 00:20:50,684
Where's Pogi?

344
00:20:51,352 --> 00:20:56,457
From now on, I will get your remittance.

345
00:20:56,457 --> 00:20:59,460
- Congressman sent me...
- He gave him the go signal.

346
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:01,529
Make sure it's safe.

347
00:21:01,529 --> 00:21:04,732
We don't want the chief to get in trouble.

348
00:21:04,732 --> 00:21:07,334
You can trust me.

349
00:21:45,573 --> 00:21:47,908
Boss, I'm begging you.

350
00:21:47,908 --> 00:21:49,243
Boss, I have a family.

351
00:21:49,243 --> 00:21:51,545
Boss, I won't talk.

352
00:21:51,545 --> 00:21:53,713
Wait, don't!

353
00:22:01,789 --> 00:22:04,858
If my brother learns that someone saw us,

354
00:22:04,858 --> 00:22:06,883
we'll be dead meat.

355
00:22:23,277 --> 00:22:25,534
When I read Liam's script,

356
00:22:25,534 --> 00:22:29,933
I thought,
"Wait! There's something I can change."

357
00:22:29,933 --> 00:22:33,586
I can make your movie better.

358
00:22:33,586 --> 00:22:39,236
So Queenie, show them the wardrobe
I handpicked for the female lead.

359
00:22:39,236 --> 00:22:41,961
Straight from Paris, Mademoiselle.

360
00:22:41,961 --> 00:22:45,465
These are the outfits for the scenes
where the couple is still happy.

361
00:22:45,465 --> 00:22:48,968
Flowy, romantic dress.

362
00:22:48,968 --> 00:22:52,127
I'll wear it if you don't want it, Miss Joyce.

363
00:22:54,242 --> 00:22:56,664
Via, isn't this too much? I feel shy.

364
00:22:57,346 --> 00:23:02,949
I'm actually forcing Liam
to include me in your project.

365
00:23:02,949 --> 00:23:07,634
I'm the one embarrassed that
I'm forcing myself here.

366
00:23:08,508 --> 00:23:10,446
It's not like that, love.

367
00:23:10,446 --> 00:23:13,493
I just thought you were busy in Escale.

368
00:23:14,527 --> 00:23:16,295
I'm not.

369
00:23:17,367 --> 00:23:20,665
I want to join you in this project.

370
00:23:20,665 --> 00:23:24,769
Is your dream exclusive
only for the two of you?

371
00:23:24,769 --> 00:23:26,337
Of course not.

372
00:23:26,337 --> 00:23:33,964
You're also part of my life...
of my... dreams.

373
00:23:36,238 --> 00:23:37,850
So?

374
00:23:37,850 --> 00:23:42,320
Does it mean the wardrobe I presented
is already approved,

375
00:23:42,320 --> 00:23:45,331
Mr. Creative Manager?

376
00:23:53,011 --> 00:23:56,869
Joyce, someone's looking for you.

377
00:23:56,869 --> 00:23:58,471
Hans.

378
00:23:58,471 --> 00:23:59,871
Hello.

379
00:24:02,074 --> 00:24:05,353
Your boyfriend is good-looking.

380
00:24:05,353 --> 00:24:08,320
True. That's true, Mama Tess.

381
00:24:10,750 --> 00:24:13,604
Aunt Tess, this is Hans.

382
00:24:14,587 --> 00:24:16,055
My friend.

383
00:24:16,055 --> 00:24:17,557
He's a lawyer.

384
00:24:18,926 --> 00:24:20,995
Hi, Attorney.

385
00:24:20,995 --> 00:24:23,067
Hot-ttorney.

386
00:24:25,865 --> 00:24:29,337
You two look good together.

387
00:24:29,337 --> 00:24:35,074
You're like Liam and Via.
The chemistry is perfect.

388
00:24:37,724 --> 00:24:40,193
What are you doing here?

389
00:24:41,349 --> 00:24:44,596
Did you forget? You asked me to pick you up.

390
00:24:46,287 --> 00:24:49,307
I'm so sorry I forgot.

391
00:24:50,862 --> 00:24:52,489
Are you still finishing something?

392
00:24:52,489 --> 00:24:54,362
It's okay. I can wait.

393
00:24:54,362 --> 00:24:57,064
Are... are we done?

394
00:24:58,164 --> 00:24:59,732
Yeah, I think so.

395
00:24:59,732 --> 00:25:01,835
Joyce is already free, Hans.

396
00:25:01,835 --> 00:25:03,745
Right, love?

397
00:25:05,071 --> 00:25:06,645
Yeah, we're done.

398
00:25:06,645 --> 00:25:08,026
We're finished.

399
00:25:14,747 --> 00:25:18,250
Excuse me. Sorry. I need to take this call.

400
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:24,997
Via, I'm happy that you and Liam
will work together.

401
00:25:24,997 --> 00:25:28,120
Me, too, Auntie. I'm glad he hired me.

402
00:25:28,828 --> 00:25:30,229
You're more than capable, Via.

403
00:25:30,229 --> 00:25:32,965
I even made a presentation and everything.

404
00:25:32,965 --> 00:25:34,801
Okay, okay.

405
00:25:34,801 --> 00:25:36,534
Thank you. Bye.

406
00:25:39,300 --> 00:25:41,835
Hans, you're all good?

407
00:25:45,151 --> 00:25:46,718
Liam...

408
00:25:48,141 --> 00:25:51,187
Your family owns Casa Fuerte, right?

409
00:25:53,453 --> 00:25:55,594
Yes. My dad is the CEO.

410
00:25:55,594 --> 00:25:57,265
Why?

411
00:25:57,265 --> 00:26:00,522
An accident happened at
your construction site.

412
00:26:01,227 --> 00:26:02,495
Wait.

413
00:26:02,495 --> 00:26:03,828
Oh, my God.

414
00:26:03,828 --> 00:26:05,695
Accident?

415
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:09,816
Did someone die at Casa Fuerte?

416
00:26:11,154 --> 00:26:13,717
Involving a construction worker.

417
00:26:37,365 --> 00:26:40,867
My friend, what's going on?

418
00:26:40,867 --> 00:26:43,336
I did what you told me.

419
00:26:43,336 --> 00:26:46,339
I put some of the money in Casa Fuerte.

420
00:26:46,339 --> 00:26:49,008
And some in Blacksmith.

421
00:26:49,008 --> 00:26:51,156
We don't have a problem anymore.

422
00:26:51,156 --> 00:26:53,812
It's all clean. We're now in the clear.

423
00:26:58,786 --> 00:27:03,289
My friend, I did everything
you told me to do.

424
00:27:03,289 --> 00:27:04,889
Someone saw you.

425
00:27:04,889 --> 00:27:06,192
Boss, I have a family.

426
00:27:06,192 --> 00:27:07,622
I won't talk.

427
00:27:07,622 --> 00:27:12,699
We'll be dead if Big bro learns
that someone else saw us.

428
00:27:12,699 --> 00:27:15,634
Big bro, I got of rid of him already.

429
00:27:26,043 --> 00:27:27,745
Big bro.

430
00:27:35,054 --> 00:27:37,357
You didn't cover your tracks.

431
00:27:37,357 --> 00:27:40,493
- The construction worker...
- He's already dead, right?

432
00:27:40,493 --> 00:27:42,195
He's alive!

433
00:27:42,195 --> 00:27:44,275
And still breathing.

434
00:27:45,765 --> 00:27:49,335
I should also kill people like you.

435
00:27:49,335 --> 00:27:52,154
I'm surrounded by stupid people!

436
00:27:52,154 --> 00:27:53,822
Don't.

437
00:27:55,274 --> 00:27:57,576
Spare me, Ramon.

438
00:27:58,476 --> 00:28:00,911
I'm a newbie.

439
00:28:03,779 --> 00:28:07,183
That's why I need veterans.

440
00:28:15,895 --> 00:28:18,090
This is Lando.

441
00:28:18,898 --> 00:28:22,012
My most trusted gunman.

442
00:28:23,436 --> 00:28:30,943
That face is the last thing you'll see
if you fail again, Danilo.

443
00:28:39,552 --> 00:28:43,656
I won't call you if it's not urgent.

444
00:28:43,656 --> 00:28:45,621
Anytime, Big bro.

445
00:29:00,841 --> 00:29:04,610
Dear, why did you let Joyce
make an independent film?

446
00:29:04,610 --> 00:29:07,013
Who will watch that?

447
00:29:07,013 --> 00:29:08,715
I didn't allow her.

448
00:29:08,715 --> 00:29:11,067
She's just stubborn.

449
00:29:11,067 --> 00:29:14,120
Indie, my foot.
She won't make money off of that.

450
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:15,911
Correct.

451
00:29:15,911 --> 00:29:19,584
And those who do independent films
are the has-beens.

452
00:29:19,584 --> 00:29:23,529
Yes, there are awards.
But there's no money on that.

453
00:29:23,529 --> 00:29:24,530
Correct.

454
00:29:24,530 --> 00:29:27,036
- You won't gain profit from it.
- True.

455
00:29:28,201 --> 00:29:31,178
Mommy, I have good news.

456
00:29:33,072 --> 00:29:37,944
DigiTV has already agreed
to produce our indie film.

457
00:29:37,944 --> 00:29:40,603
I hope you change your mind.

458
00:29:41,802 --> 00:29:44,221
We need to talk.

459
00:29:49,881 --> 00:29:52,316
Aren't you happy?

460
00:29:54,512 --> 00:29:55,897
What's this?

461
00:29:55,897 --> 00:29:58,167
[Falling Star?
Joyce A.K.A. Savana Dropped by Blacksmith]

462
00:30:02,702 --> 00:30:06,269
You're still against it?
You won't support me?

463
00:30:06,269 --> 00:30:10,042
Liam has poisoned your mind, hasn't he?

464
00:30:10,042 --> 00:30:12,500
Oh my God!

465
00:30:12,501 --> 00:30:15,434
Why did you have to get

466
00:30:15,434 --> 00:30:18,856
the black sheep of the Herreras
for a boyfriend?

467
00:30:18,856 --> 00:30:21,605
I wish you got Vergil instead.

468
00:30:28,406 --> 00:30:30,507
Is this still about money?

469
00:30:32,698 --> 00:30:37,804
Are you still thinking about money, Mom?

470
00:30:37,804 --> 00:30:41,440
I noticed you always say that to me.

471
00:30:41,440 --> 00:30:44,011
What do you take me for? Greedy for money?

472
00:30:44,011 --> 00:30:46,180
This is not about money.

473
00:30:46,180 --> 00:30:48,482
This is about your career.

474
00:30:48,482 --> 00:30:51,251
Do you believe that's what people think?

475
00:30:51,251 --> 00:30:52,986
Look at the comment section.

476
00:30:52,986 --> 00:30:54,321
They're bashing you.

477
00:30:54,321 --> 00:30:57,957
I am tired of pleasing people, Mom!

478
00:30:58,692 --> 00:31:01,383
I'm so sick of it.

479
00:31:03,701 --> 00:31:06,704
I don't care about what they think.

480
00:31:07,868 --> 00:31:11,578
I don't care about what they say.

481
00:31:14,007 --> 00:31:16,343
I'm old enough.

482
00:31:16,343 --> 00:31:20,079
I can think on my own, Mom.

483
00:31:24,891 --> 00:31:30,457
I'm so tired of being controlled,

484
00:31:30,457 --> 00:31:34,193
on how to portray this and that.

485
00:31:36,530 --> 00:31:43,269
I don't want anyone telling me
to say things against my will.

486
00:31:44,839 --> 00:31:49,544
I'm so tired, Mom,

487
00:31:49,544 --> 00:31:55,383
of being told to believe stories
that I can't find any worth.

488
00:31:58,987 --> 00:32:02,810
That's the reason I cannot let go of you.

489
00:32:03,692 --> 00:32:07,646
Because I can see that you're still immature.

490
00:32:10,396 --> 00:32:12,514
Remember this.

491
00:32:13,532 --> 00:32:19,201
You stepped on me,
that's why you're not on the ground.

492
00:32:19,201 --> 00:32:22,639
You wouldn't have all of this
if it wasn't for me.

493
00:32:23,680 --> 00:32:28,250
That's why all your decisions
should go through me.

494
00:32:30,967 --> 00:32:33,118
Fine.

495
00:32:33,118 --> 00:32:36,255
I will let you indulge in your craziness.

496
00:32:37,222 --> 00:32:40,350
But the next time you sign a contract,

497
00:32:40,350 --> 00:32:44,653
you will sign it
even if it comes from a demon!

498
00:32:53,641 --> 00:32:55,974
What happened?

499
00:32:59,714 --> 00:33:01,850
I don't need you in my movie.

500
00:33:01,850 --> 00:33:05,353
There are lots of women
prettier and sexier than you.

501
00:33:05,353 --> 00:33:06,888
Director, wait.

502
00:33:06,888 --> 00:33:08,099
What happened?

503
00:33:08,099 --> 00:33:11,726
Wait. Wait, Director.
I will talk to my daughter.

504
00:33:11,726 --> 00:33:15,027
Joyce, why did he get mad at you?

505
00:33:15,027 --> 00:33:18,096
Did he really have the guts to get mad, Mom?

506
00:33:18,096 --> 00:33:20,901
He harassed me!

507
00:33:23,314 --> 00:33:27,375
Joyce! I did everything to get you a slot
in this audition.

508
00:33:27,375 --> 00:33:28,861
Come on!

509
00:33:28,861 --> 00:33:31,244
You haven't had projects for a long time now.

510
00:33:31,244 --> 00:33:32,781
Our savings are gone.

511
00:33:32,781 --> 00:33:35,950
You should just put up with it.

512
00:33:38,820 --> 00:33:41,388
So that means...

513
00:33:42,257 --> 00:33:45,426
you know he's a pervert?

514
00:33:45,426 --> 00:33:46,924
Come on, Joyce!

515
00:33:46,924 --> 00:33:49,397
If you can't swallow things like that,

516
00:33:49,397 --> 00:33:52,245
I don't know how to make you famous anymore!

517
00:33:52,245 --> 00:33:54,747
Why, Mom? Am I not capable?

518
00:33:55,937 --> 00:33:57,305
Am I not that good to you?

519
00:33:57,305 --> 00:34:01,442
Can't I decently get a job?

520
00:34:03,411 --> 00:34:07,198
Joyce, stay here.

521
00:34:07,198 --> 00:34:09,559
Wait for me.

522
00:34:09,559 --> 00:34:11,786
I'll talk to the director.

523
00:34:11,786 --> 00:34:14,989
I will ask him to let you audition.

524
00:34:14,989 --> 00:34:17,219
But I'll be there. I will look out for you.

525
00:34:17,219 --> 00:34:18,293
You can do this.

526
00:34:18,293 --> 00:34:19,627
You can do this. Wait for me.

527
00:34:19,627 --> 00:34:22,563
Director! Director!

528
00:34:53,215 --> 00:34:55,330
Where were we?

529
00:34:55,330 --> 00:34:58,430
Hi, hello.

530
00:34:58,430 --> 00:35:00,001
Oh, dear. Are you okay?

531
00:35:00,001 --> 00:35:01,389
Yeah, of course.

532
00:35:01,389 --> 00:35:03,171
We're okay too.

533
00:35:03,171 --> 00:35:05,606
You know me, right?

534
00:35:09,048 --> 00:35:11,770
I'm glad you met with me.

535
00:35:15,881 --> 00:35:17,520
Dad...

536
00:35:19,020 --> 00:35:23,555
I know I caused big trouble
when I left Casa Fuerte and Blacksmith.

537
00:35:24,668 --> 00:35:31,351
So I'll understand
if you see me as a big disappointment.

538
00:35:32,786 --> 00:35:36,756
But I am here because I'm worried about you.

539
00:35:38,845 --> 00:35:40,208
Dad, please tell me.

540
00:35:40,208 --> 00:35:43,912
What happened to the construction worker
who got into an accident?

541
00:35:43,912 --> 00:35:47,431
Liam, it's out of your concern.

542
00:35:47,431 --> 00:35:50,082
You said so yourself.

543
00:35:50,082 --> 00:35:54,137
You abandoned me when you left Casa Fuerte.

544
00:35:54,137 --> 00:35:55,723
So, please...

545
00:35:55,723 --> 00:35:59,315
Please stop doing the wrong things.

546
00:35:59,315 --> 00:36:00,795
Wrong?

547
00:36:00,795 --> 00:36:05,400
What's right and wrong when
someone's life is on the line?

548
00:36:05,400 --> 00:36:08,603
My friend, I did everything
you told me to do.

549
00:36:08,603 --> 00:36:11,004
This is Lando.

550
00:36:11,915 --> 00:36:14,390
My most trusted gunman.

551
00:36:14,390 --> 00:36:21,515
That face is the last thing you'll see
if you fail again, Danilo.

552
00:36:28,695 --> 00:36:35,261
The construction worker was sleeping
at the site without permission, Liam.

553
00:36:35,261 --> 00:36:37,830
But someone told me he was shot.

554
00:36:37,830 --> 00:36:39,465
Please.

555
00:36:39,465 --> 00:36:41,634
I don't want to fight over this.

556
00:36:41,634 --> 00:36:47,739
Casa Fuerte will pay for all the expenses
needed for his recovery.

557
00:36:49,405 --> 00:36:52,040
I really hope you're okay, Dad.

558
00:36:53,112 --> 00:36:56,849
Dad, it's not too late.

559
00:36:56,849 --> 00:36:59,959
For you, for us.

560
00:36:59,959 --> 00:37:02,429
We can still break free
from Congressman Ramon.

561
00:37:02,429 --> 00:37:04,197
Liam...

562
00:37:05,757 --> 00:37:09,460
I know I wasn't the best father
for you and your brother.

563
00:37:11,164 --> 00:37:13,999
But someday...

564
00:37:14,696 --> 00:37:17,231
you'll understand...

565
00:37:19,412 --> 00:37:23,294
that I became a father the way I know how.

566
00:37:40,693 --> 00:37:44,498
What do you want? Bihon or Palabok?

567
00:37:44,498 --> 00:37:46,299
- Palabok.
- Palabok.

568
00:37:46,299 --> 00:37:49,002
- Here you go.
- Excuse me, here's the barbecue.

569
00:37:49,002 --> 00:37:50,070
- Oh, wow!
- Let me have it.

570
00:37:50,070 --> 00:37:51,905
Give it to me.

571
00:37:51,905 --> 00:37:54,741
Come on. Hurry up. Pass it to them.
So we can refill it again.

572
00:37:54,741 --> 00:37:57,511
- Okay. Wait, wait.
- Let's put some...

573
00:37:57,511 --> 00:38:00,347
Hey, why did you get all of it?

574
00:38:00,347 --> 00:38:02,249
Are you hungry, Borj?

575
00:38:02,249 --> 00:38:05,418
Auntie, thank you so much.

576
00:38:05,418 --> 00:38:08,288
Thank you so much for the food.

577
00:38:08,288 --> 00:38:11,191
It's a pre-filming celebration for us.

578
00:38:11,191 --> 00:38:13,437
It's nothing.

579
00:38:13,437 --> 00:38:16,951
This is our advanced victory party.

580
00:38:18,632 --> 00:38:24,371
But I notice you're quiet today.

581
00:38:24,371 --> 00:38:27,406
Aren't you excited about tomorrow?

582
00:38:34,758 --> 00:38:36,726
I'm excited.

583
00:38:38,385 --> 00:38:41,054
Maybe I'm just tired.

584
00:38:41,054 --> 00:38:43,456
You'll finish it.

585
00:38:43,456 --> 00:38:45,825
You have a good team.

586
00:38:45,825 --> 00:38:51,364
Just be professional,
and don't take it personally.

587
00:38:57,204 --> 00:38:58,972
- It's good.
- I want an egg.

588
00:38:58,972 --> 00:39:01,207
Do you like kids too?

589
00:39:03,449 --> 00:39:05,650
I'm an only child.

590
00:39:07,928 --> 00:39:11,731
But I dream of having a big family.

591
00:39:14,269 --> 00:39:16,923
You and Liam are the same.

592
00:39:16,923 --> 00:39:18,425
Solo.

593
00:39:18,425 --> 00:39:21,895
Oh, he's not alone.

594
00:39:22,996 --> 00:39:24,764
I forgot he has a brother.

595
00:39:24,764 --> 00:39:27,201
But he's stubborn.

596
00:39:29,936 --> 00:39:31,371
Try this.

597
00:39:31,371 --> 00:39:33,061
Try the barbecue.

598
00:39:33,061 --> 00:39:34,207
Thank you.

599
00:39:34,207 --> 00:39:37,110
Sir Liam, can I borrow your phone?

600
00:39:37,110 --> 00:39:39,345
Oh, this boy.

601
00:39:41,647 --> 00:39:44,117
Auntie, this is so good.

602
00:39:44,117 --> 00:39:45,389
What?

603
00:39:46,353 --> 00:39:48,955
You make good barbecue.

604
00:39:48,955 --> 00:39:51,424
You can win an award for this.

605
00:39:51,424 --> 00:39:53,126
Oh, dear.

606
00:39:53,126 --> 00:39:57,464
It really is good.

607
00:39:57,464 --> 00:39:59,432
It's not in the sauce.

608
00:39:59,432 --> 00:40:02,068
It depends on how long you marinate it...

609
00:40:02,068 --> 00:40:05,372
just like relationships.

610
00:40:05,372 --> 00:40:08,308
It gets better as it gets longer.

611
00:40:08,308 --> 00:40:12,095
- That's my barbecue.
- Like Liam and Via.

612
00:40:12,095 --> 00:40:14,033
They don't have the same attitude.

613
00:40:14,033 --> 00:40:20,286
But they complement each other
as time goes by.

614
00:40:21,655 --> 00:40:22,876
How about you?

615
00:40:22,876 --> 00:40:28,603
How's your friend Hans?

616
00:40:31,598 --> 00:40:37,470
Hans and I are both workaholics.

617
00:40:37,470 --> 00:40:41,073
That's the case, Attorney.
His story isn't consistent.

618
00:40:41,073 --> 00:40:44,827
He first told me
that there were other people that night.

619
00:40:44,827 --> 00:40:47,947
And then he said he slipped.

620
00:40:48,848 --> 00:40:50,517
Will you shut up?

621
00:40:50,517 --> 00:40:52,919
Siloy, the lawyer's here already.

622
00:40:52,919 --> 00:40:55,121
You don't have to be scared now.

623
00:40:56,523 --> 00:41:00,994
Ma'am, Sir, it's okay if
you're not ready to talk yet.

624
00:41:00,994 --> 00:41:02,495
No, Attorney.

625
00:41:02,495 --> 00:41:05,298
Yes, my husband became disabled
because of the incident.

626
00:41:05,298 --> 00:41:06,833
And we will lose our income.

627
00:41:06,833 --> 00:41:09,668
But I'm not just after the money.

628
00:41:10,537 --> 00:41:12,471
I want justice.

629
00:41:19,679 --> 00:41:22,716
We both love working.

630
00:41:22,716 --> 00:41:23,717
Is that so?

631
00:41:23,717 --> 00:41:27,220
Why don't you give him a chance?

632
00:41:27,220 --> 00:41:30,856
How will you know the taste
if you won't try it?

633
00:41:33,059 --> 00:41:35,254
I'm going to try it, Auntie?

634
00:41:35,254 --> 00:41:37,397
Auntie, I was shocked.

635
00:41:37,397 --> 00:41:39,466
That's not what I meant.

636
00:41:39,466 --> 00:41:40,900
Sorry.

637
00:41:40,900 --> 00:41:45,305
What I mean is, give him a chance.

638
00:41:45,305 --> 00:41:46,806
Who knows?

639
00:41:46,806 --> 00:41:48,707
Right?

640
00:41:50,678 --> 00:41:52,794
Oh, dear.

641
00:42:03,056 --> 00:42:04,758
Hi, love.

642
00:42:04,758 --> 00:42:06,622
- Auntie.
- Hi!

643
00:42:07,520 --> 00:42:08,561
Hello.

644
00:42:08,561 --> 00:42:10,230
Hello, too.

645
00:42:10,230 --> 00:42:12,265
- Have a seat.
- Hi.

646
00:42:12,265 --> 00:42:15,069
Give her a plate.

647
00:42:15,069 --> 00:42:18,395
Miss Via...

648
00:42:20,707 --> 00:42:25,844
Sir Liam, Miss Joyce, let's do TikTok.

649
00:42:25,844 --> 00:42:27,113
I don't know how to do TikTok.

650
00:42:27,113 --> 00:42:29,100
- I don't know how, too.
- I will teach you.

651
00:42:29,100 --> 00:42:30,606
What are the steps?

652
00:42:30,606 --> 00:42:32,051
I don't know how to dance.
What are we doing to do?

653
00:42:32,051 --> 00:42:34,287
- Go ahead. Do it.
- I don't know how to do it.

654
00:42:34,287 --> 00:42:35,455
Let's do TikTok.

655
00:42:35,455 --> 00:42:37,924
- Is it easy?
- Come on, Miss Joyce.

656
00:42:37,924 --> 00:42:39,859
Oh, no.

657
00:42:39,859 --> 00:42:42,762
- I don't know how to do it.
- Where are we going to do it?

658
00:42:42,762 --> 00:42:44,063
Sep, let's just do something easy.

659
00:42:44,063 --> 00:42:46,266
- Yes.
- He's going to teach them.

660
00:42:46,266 --> 00:42:49,436
One, two, three, go!

661
00:42:49,436 --> 00:42:51,404
Cupid's bow and arrow.

662
00:42:51,404 --> 00:42:53,072
- He hit me.
- Do you want some, Via?

663
00:42:53,072 --> 00:42:54,741
I'm already in love.

664
00:42:54,741 --> 00:42:56,825
I'm already in love.

665
00:43:03,550 --> 00:43:07,052
Miss Via, do you want to join us?

666
00:43:07,787 --> 00:43:09,589
No, thanks.

667
00:43:09,589 --> 00:43:10,990
I'm wearing high heels.

668
00:43:10,990 --> 00:43:13,259
- You can't get tired, remember?
- Yeah.

669
00:43:13,259 --> 00:43:16,094
- Let's finish the video.
- Get some rest first.

670
00:43:16,094 --> 00:43:19,166
Miss Joyce, I'll get more views
because of you.

671
00:43:19,167 --> 00:43:20,430
Are we going to...

672
00:43:20,431 --> 00:43:21,566
Fine.

673
00:43:21,567 --> 00:43:24,534
- You're getting sweaty.
- You need to rest. You can't get tired.

674
00:43:24,534 --> 00:43:29,908
Cupid's bow and arrow.
I think I fell in love with you.

675
00:43:29,908 --> 00:43:33,012
You know what? Mom, join us.

676
00:43:33,012 --> 00:43:34,147
I don't know how to do that.

677
00:43:34,147 --> 00:43:36,616
Come on. Don't be shy.
I can see you're dancing.

678
00:43:36,616 --> 00:43:38,284
Not really.

679
00:43:38,284 --> 00:43:40,085
Come here.

680
00:43:40,085 --> 00:43:42,567
Let's not do that. I don't know how to do it.

681
00:43:42,567 --> 00:43:45,153
Auntie, I didn't know you liked TikTok.

682
00:43:45,153 --> 00:43:46,359
You even do Zumba.

683
00:43:46,359 --> 00:43:48,595
Hey, don't say that in front of your friends.

684
00:43:48,595 --> 00:43:50,489
That's embarrassing.

685
00:44:15,655 --> 00:44:17,856
<i>Thank you, Grandma.</i>

686
00:44:20,293 --> 00:44:22,695
<i>Are you happy?</i>

687
00:44:26,165 --> 00:44:27,734
Daddy, look. Balloons.

688
00:44:27,734 --> 00:44:29,068
Balloons!

689
00:44:29,068 --> 00:44:33,240
I didn't bring money with me.

690
00:44:33,240 --> 00:44:34,374
I'll buy it.

691
00:44:34,374 --> 00:44:37,210
Come here. How many do you want?

692
00:44:37,210 --> 00:44:38,745
Three.

693
00:44:38,745 --> 00:44:41,214
Go on and pick. What color do you want?

694
00:44:41,214 --> 00:44:42,549
Red.

695
00:44:42,549 --> 00:44:44,183
- Red.
- I want three of them.

696
00:44:44,183 --> 00:44:47,687
My grandchild wants the red balloons.

697
00:44:47,687 --> 00:44:50,356
Mister, three red balloons, please.

698
00:44:51,057 --> 00:44:53,993
Here it is. Keep the change, okay?

699
00:44:53,993 --> 00:44:55,778
Thank you, Grandma.

700
00:44:55,778 --> 00:44:58,831
You're welcome, my grandson.

701
00:44:58,831 --> 00:45:00,833
- Are you happy?
- Mama Tess, thank you.

702
00:45:00,833 --> 00:45:03,336
I love you, Grandma.

703
00:45:03,336 --> 00:45:05,238
I love you.

704
00:45:05,238 --> 00:45:07,072
I love you too.

705
00:45:08,075 --> 00:45:10,510
Are you now happy with your balloons?

706
00:45:10,510 --> 00:45:12,299
Yes.

707
00:45:17,850 --> 00:45:19,452
Mom?

708
00:45:19,452 --> 00:45:20,687
Mom. Mom.

709
00:45:20,687 --> 00:45:22,088
Mom, are you okay?

710
00:45:22,088 --> 00:45:23,922
What happened?

711
00:45:25,592 --> 00:45:26,793
I'm okay, son.

712
00:45:26,793 --> 00:45:29,063
- What?
- I just felt a bit dizzy.

713
00:45:29,063 --> 00:45:31,392
Do you want me to bring you to the hospital?

714
00:45:31,392 --> 00:45:33,132
No, there's no need. I'm okay.

715
00:45:33,132 --> 00:45:34,901
- You look like you need...
- Continue what you're doing.

716
00:45:34,901 --> 00:45:36,135
I'll just take some rest.

717
00:45:36,135 --> 00:45:37,537
Auntie, are you okay?

718
00:45:37,537 --> 00:45:39,671
Are you okay?

719
00:45:40,640 --> 00:45:43,242
Yes, I'm okay.

720
00:45:43,242 --> 00:45:44,644
Guys, sorry.

721
00:45:44,644 --> 00:45:48,581
I think I should bring my mom home.

722
00:45:48,581 --> 00:45:50,950
Go ahead, Liam.
We'll take care of everything here.

723
00:45:50,950 --> 00:45:53,152
It's okay.

724
00:45:53,152 --> 00:45:55,989
Aunt Tess, are you really okay?

725
00:45:55,989 --> 00:45:57,329
Yeah.

726
00:45:58,182 --> 00:46:01,928
Yes, son. I think you should bring me home.

727
00:46:01,928 --> 00:46:04,330
I'll get some rest at home.

728
00:46:04,330 --> 00:46:05,864
Okay.

729
00:46:08,593 --> 00:46:12,062
We can't talk to anyone from Casa Fuerte.

730
00:46:15,508 --> 00:46:19,873
What will you do with justice
if it brings you trouble?

731
00:46:19,873 --> 00:46:22,742
That's why Attorney's here.

732
00:46:25,985 --> 00:46:30,189
Maybe I should come back some other day.

733
00:46:30,189 --> 00:46:32,125
It's okay.

734
00:46:32,125 --> 00:46:35,161
Attorney, I'm sorry for wasting your time.

735
00:46:35,161 --> 00:46:36,496
No.

736
00:46:36,496 --> 00:46:40,533
You don't have to apologize.
It's okay. Get well soon.

737
00:46:40,533 --> 00:46:43,603
Just call me when you're ready to talk.

738
00:46:43,603 --> 00:46:45,404
Thank you.

739
00:46:47,108 --> 00:46:49,476
I'll get going, Sir.

740
00:47:02,522 --> 00:47:07,727
Ma'am, I can see
that your husband doesn't want to talk.

741
00:47:07,727 --> 00:47:12,164
And I understand
because I'm a stranger to him.

742
00:47:12,877 --> 00:47:17,717
But I'll do what I can
to find out what really happened.

743
00:47:17,717 --> 00:47:20,740
I'll find out if someone has to pay
for what happened to your husband.

744
00:47:20,741 --> 00:47:23,910
Thank you, Attorney. I'll count on you.

745
00:47:24,911 --> 00:47:27,080
Okay. Just call me.

746
00:47:27,080 --> 00:47:30,511
- I'll get going.
- Be safe. Thank you.

747
00:47:40,439 --> 00:47:43,241
You can leave me alone, son.

748
00:47:43,915 --> 00:47:47,103
This is getting offensive.

749
00:47:47,103 --> 00:47:49,068
I'm still young.

750
00:47:49,068 --> 00:47:52,605
Mom, we're not talking about age here.

751
00:47:52,605 --> 00:47:54,815
But your health.

752
00:47:54,815 --> 00:47:58,444
How about it? Let's go to the hospital?

753
00:47:58,444 --> 00:48:00,947
You're so serious.

754
00:48:00,947 --> 00:48:06,586
Maybe I just got dizzy
because it was so hot at the park earlier.

755
00:48:06,586 --> 00:48:07,737
That's all.

756
00:48:07,737 --> 00:48:10,757
You're so stubborn.

757
00:48:10,757 --> 00:48:13,592
I give up.

758
00:48:16,694 --> 00:48:17,731
But you know what, son?

759
00:48:17,734 --> 00:48:19,699
Earlier...

760
00:48:21,691 --> 00:48:23,992
I felt like I was dreaming.

761
00:48:27,106 --> 00:48:29,007
I saw you...

762
00:48:30,741 --> 00:48:33,156
Joyce...

763
00:48:33,156 --> 00:48:35,157
and Sep.

764
00:48:37,084 --> 00:48:40,275
You and Joyce are husband and wife.

765
00:48:40,275 --> 00:48:43,110
You're a family.

766
00:48:45,946 --> 00:48:50,329
W-What's that? Am I hallucinating?

767
00:48:50,329 --> 00:48:55,567
Or you were so focused
on Joyce and Sep earlier.

768
00:48:55,567 --> 00:48:57,569
That's why?

769
00:49:02,008 --> 00:49:04,143
Come on, Mom.

770
00:49:04,143 --> 00:49:08,947
Maybe you've watched too many drama series.

771
00:49:09,782 --> 00:49:16,054
And Joyce already has Hans.

772
00:49:17,030 --> 00:49:18,591
And I...

773
00:49:18,591 --> 00:49:20,392
You have Via.

774
00:49:21,661 --> 00:49:24,896
Okay. Maybe I really should get some rest.

775
00:49:27,166 --> 00:49:28,301
Go on, Mom.

776
00:49:28,301 --> 00:49:29,435
Go to sleep now.

777
00:49:29,435 --> 00:49:32,350
I'll stay here. I'll watch over you.

778
00:49:32,350 --> 00:49:35,007
Go on, you can leave. I'm okay.

779
00:49:35,007 --> 00:49:37,510
Close your eyes now.

780
00:49:37,510 --> 00:49:39,061
Oh, boy.

781
00:50:02,935 --> 00:50:04,837
Welcome back to my private resort.

782
00:50:04,837 --> 00:50:08,608
Mayor, thank you so much
for letting us film here.

783
00:50:08,608 --> 00:50:10,176
I can't say no to Via.

784
00:50:10,176 --> 00:50:11,958
And speaking of Via...

785
00:50:11,958 --> 00:50:13,479
I'm so sorry we're late.

786
00:50:13,479 --> 00:50:15,081
Why do you look so surprised?

787
00:50:15,081 --> 00:50:16,782
Sir Liam's script is really something.

788
00:50:16,782 --> 00:50:19,825
It feels like it can move mountains.

789
00:50:19,825 --> 00:50:22,488
It shows that he's so in love.

790
00:50:22,488 --> 00:50:25,192
The question is, with whom is he in love?

791
00:50:25,192 --> 00:50:29,434
Even the happiest film ends.

792
00:50:39,805 --> 00:50:42,213
I heard that Siloy is dead.

793
00:50:44,377 --> 00:50:45,687
What the...

794
00:50:45,687 --> 00:50:47,080
<i>Joyce, where are you?</i>

795
00:50:47,080 --> 00:50:50,649
<i>Your dad collapsed in his house.</i>
